I'm a computer science graduate from Chulalongkorn University who works where AI, data and real business problems meet. My job is to listen to what a team needs, then build the tool that solves it, whether that's an AI agent, a web app or a data pipeline.

I started in research, co-authoring VerteRo, a deep learning tool for spine X-rays published in *Global Spine Journal*. I then worked as a data engineer building pipelines in Databricks. Today I'm a Management Trainee at P.S.P. Specialties, building automation for planning, accounts payable and distribution teams.

I use AI in almost everything I build, and I care about understanding how the models actually work, from classic ML to deep learning and LLMs.
